/-! Production API: Ixon v3 ingress, the shared semantic vocabulary, the Src
front end (ingress, the checked unfolding table, SrcEval, relevance), global and
constructor keys, Lam with level-exact, keyed erasure from Src, Anf with the
Phase 1 middle end (P1–P4), first-order Fir lowered from Anf, the Phase 1
(immortal) Own fragment with its checker, Cfg with its small-step semantics
and the lowering from Own, the Phase 1 runtime (`Rt.lower` from Cfg to Lir
with the immortal bump allocator, `cx_init` and the `Nat` procedures, and
typed readback), Lir (the backend's first IR), Xv and Xl (x86 instructions over virtual registers and
over locations) with rule-based selection from Lir, register allocation
(linear scan, the all-slots fallback and the kernel-evaluable validator),
stacking (frames, the SysV export wrapper and the exit group) and block layout
down to typed x86 (`Backend.emit`), the x86 target model with its certified
encoder (E1) and stream/ELF layer (E2), the compiler itself (`Recheck`: the
certificate, `produce`, the recheck path `Recheck.run` and `compile`, and the
front half's refinement from the checked source to the loaded Lir program,
`Recheck.front_refines`, the backend half's (`Recheck.back_refines`: the object
run by the runtime driver, `X86.Linked`, refines the loaded Lir program), and
the correctness statement at stage S for every object `Recheck.run` makes (`Recheck.sound`); `Cli`:
the `ixcc` command line; `Exe`: standalone executables of a root, with `X86.Exe`'s shell, layout,
executable writer and check, and of numeric state machines, with `Exe.Machine`'s interface and
session model (the session theorem, `Exe.Machine.Sound`, is in the proof collection) and
`X86.Exe.Machine`'s generic shell), and the Aiur target. The compiler pipeline is being rebuilt; see
`docs/roadmap.md`. The complete regression and proof collection is built explicitly through
`IxCCTests.Proofs`. The checked plain-RC companion API is
`Recheck.RcReplay`: complete ownership certificate serialization/replay,
allocation/reclamation/recycling lowering, emitted ELF and raw-word `cx_drop`.
Its separate proof modules extend the SrcEval-relative statement to the
admitted heap fragment while preserving the existing source and driver
qualifications. -/
